From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 21:25:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 43/57] LOCAL: pvr: ISP merge values on parameter format v1

Local test patch for the GE8300 (22.68.54.30) on amazon-sheldonp; not to
be sent. Mesa leaves the HWRT ISP merge bounds and scales at zero on
roguexe cores with 16x16 tiles, but Fire OS's DDK (libsrv_um.so,
RGXAddRenderTarget) computes them for this core with the same formulas.
With zeros, triangles that write depth (PDS triangle merging enabled)
were all dropped.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c
index 36641d519e9..bc859ab0a61 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_job_render.c
@@ -563,8 +563,13 @@ static void pvr_rt_dataset_ws_create_info_init(
    create_info->layers = rt_dataset->layers;
 
    /* ISP register values. */
+   /* The DDK computes these on simple parameter format v1 too (GE8300);
+    * without them, PDS triangle merging drops depth-writing triangles.
+    */
    if (PVR_HAS_ENHANCEMENT(dev_info, 42307) &&
-       !(PVR_HAS_FEATURE(dev_info, roguexe) && mtile_info->tile_size_x == 16)) {
+       (!(PVR_HAS_FEATURE(dev_info, roguexe) && mtile_info->tile_size_x == 16) ||
+        PVR_GET_FEATURE_VALUE(dev_info, simple_parameter_format_version, 0) ==
+           1)) {
       float value;
 
       if (rt_dataset->width != 0) {
